# Shared gates. This file is normative after compilation, not executable code.
graph CORE 1
entry CORE-001

gate CORE-001
context TASK_START
question "Is the admitted work one clear change with a known scope and owner?"
evidence admission,scope
YES CORE-002
NO HARD-STOP-SCOPE
UNKNOWN HARD-STOP-EVIDENCE
NOT_APPLICABLE HARD-STOP-EVIDENCE
end

gate CORE-002
context TASK_START
question "Do the source, worktree, session, goal, and environment all identify the same work?"
evidence source,worktree,session,goal,environment
YES CORE-003
NO HARD-STOP-IDENTITY
UNKNOWN HARD-STOP-EVIDENCE
NOT_APPLICABLE HARD-STOP-EVIDENCE
end

gate CORE-003
context HANDOFF
question "Did the work stay inside its boundary and receive the required independent review?"
evidence changed_scope,review
YES COMPLETE
NO SOFT-REVIEW
UNKNOWN UNPROVEN
NOT_APPLICABLE SOFT-REVIEW
end

terminal COMPLETE COMPLETE "The governed work passed its applicable gates."
terminal HARD-STOP-SCOPE HARD_STOP "The scope or authority is not safe to continue."
terminal HARD-STOP-IDENTITY HARD_STOP "The work identity does not match its evidence."
terminal HARD-STOP-EVIDENCE HARD_STOP "Required evidence is missing or unknown."
terminal SOFT-REVIEW SOFT_REVIEW "An orchestrator review is required before continuing."
terminal UNPROVEN UNPROVEN "The result is not proven by the available evidence."

